{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/3131","id":3369374959,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz887I1JTv","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3131","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3131.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/3131.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/3131","number":3131,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add prominent warning banner for non-standard IP prefixes","user":{"login":"TanayK07","id":95276223,"node_id":"U_kgDOBa3Mvw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/95276223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07","html_url":"https://github.com/TanayK07","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TanayK07/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Closes #3055\r\nCloses #3062\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\n- Adds a reusable `warnBanner()` function that prints a large ASCII-art \"Warning!\" banner to the log output, matching the format from #3055\r\n- Modifies `prefixV4()` and `prefixV6()` to return a boolean indicating whether the configured prefix is outside the standard range, instead of logging independently\r\n- Consolidates the check in `LoadServerConfig()` so the banner fires **once** even if both prefixes are non-standard\r\n- Updates `config-example.yaml` to clarify that subsets of the default ranges are fine, but ranges outside CGNAT/ULA are not\r\n\r\n## What the warning looks like\r\n\r\nWhen a user configures a prefix outside the standard CGNAT or ULA range, they'll see something like this at startup:\r\n\r\n```\r\n################################################################\r\n###      __          __              _             _         ###\r\n###      \\ \\        / /             (_)           | |        ###\r\n###       \\ \\  /\\  / /_ _ _ __ _ __  _ _ __   __ _| |        ###\r\n###        \\ \\/  \\/ / _` | '__| '_ \\| | '_ \\ / _` | |        ###\r\n###         \\  /\\  / (_| | |  | | | | | | | | (_| |_|        ###\r\n###          \\/  \\/ \\__,_|_|  |_| |_|_|_| |_|\\__, (_)        ###\r\n###                                           __/ |          ###\r\n###                                          |___/           ###\r\n################################################################\r\n###                                                          ###\r\n###  You have overridden the default Headscale IP prefixes   ###\r\n###  with a range outside of the standard CGNAT and/or ULA   ###\r\n###  ranges. This is NOT a supported configuration.          ###\r\n###                                                          ###\r\n###  Using subsets of the default ranges (100.64.0.0/10 for  ###\r\n###  IPv4, fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48 for IPv6) is fine. Using      ###\r\n###  ranges outside of these will cause undefined behaviour   ###\r\n###  as the Tailscale client is NOT designed to operate on    ###\r\n###  any other ranges.                                        ###\r\n###                                                          ###\r\n###  Please revert your prefixes to subsets of the standard  ###\r\n###  ranges as described in the example configuration.        ###\r\n###                                                          ###\r\n###  Any issue raised using a range outside of the supported ###\r\n###  range will be labelled as wontfix and closed.            ###\r\n###                                                          ###\r\n################################################################\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Design decisions\r\n\r\n- **`warnBanner()` is reusable** — takes `[]string` lines and formats them into the banner box, so it can be used for other critical warnings in the future\r\n- **Warning fires once** — even if both v4 and v6 are non-standard, only one banner is printed (per review feedback on #3062)\r\n- **Subsets are fine** — the check uses `ContainsPrefix` which correctly allows subsets like `100.64.0.0/24` within the CGNAT range\r\n\r\n## Test plan\r\n\r\n- [x] Standard prefixes (100.64.0.0/10, fd7a:115c:a1e0::/48) → no warning\r\n- [x] Subset of standard range (e.g., 100.64.0.0/24) → no warning\r\n- [x] Non-standard prefix (e.g., 10.0.0.0/8) → warning banner printed\r\n- [x] Both prefixes non-standard → single warning banner\r\n- [x] Existing tests continue to pass","created_at":"2026-03-08T07:09:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T06:08:35Z","closed_at":"2026-03-19T06:08:35Z","merged_at":"2026-03-19T06:08:35Z","merge_commit_sha":"568baf3d021bd179ee3c230323984b81c7fc19a6","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://